  "interpretation": [
    "Two singleton authors have no within-author variation and contribute no author-within slope information; excluding low-count authors checks a distinct concern from the existing equal-author weighting analysis.",
    "Few posts per author does not mechanically invalidate OLS author fixed effects; slope estimates rely on within-author variation, and rare indicators can be supported by substantially fewer than 100 authors.",
    "Observed post counts are within this course sample, not complete lifetime author activity.",
    "The original main model already includes hashtag presence; controlling selected tag identities retains original body-only measurement and remains observational.",
    "Appending tags changes the text construct and turns prompt phrases into measured words; results cannot establish that original body expressions have those associations.",
    "Supplementary five-test BH adjustments are within each model, not a single correction across all exploratory model/term comparisons."
  ],
